    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Step 1: Understand the relationship between the cube and the inscribed sphere.\nFor a sphere to be inscribed in a cube, the diameter of the sphere must be equal to the edge length of the cube. In this case, the edge length of the cube is given as 6 inches.\n\nStep 2: Determine the radius of the inscribed sphere.\nSince the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube, the diameter of the sphere is 6 inches. Therefore, the radius of the sphere is half of the diameter, which is 6 inches divided by 2, resulting in a radius of 3 inches.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the volume of the inscribed sphere.\nThe formula for the volume of a sphere is given by:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3 \\]\nwhere \\( r \\) represents the radius of the sphere.\n\nStep 4: Substitute the radius into the formula.\nGiven that the radius \\( r \\) is 3 inches, substitute \\( r = 3 \\) into the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3 \\]\n\nStep 5: Perform the calculation.\nCalculate \\( 3^3 \\):\n\\[ 3^3 = 27 \\]\nNow substitute this value back into the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27 \\]\n\nStep 6: Simplify the expression.\n\\[ V = \\frac{4 \\times 27}{3} \\pi \\]\n\\[ V = \\frac{108}{3} \\pi \\]\n\\[ V = 36 \\pi \\]\n\nHence, the volume of the inscribed sphere is \\(\\boxed{36\\pi}\\) cubic inches.",
